  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">First Road Infrastructure and Maintenance Program</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Programa de Infraestructura y Conservacin Vial</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">El objetivo general de la Lnea de Crdito es contribuir al aumento de lacompetitividad y de la integracin econmica y social de la poblacin. El CCLIP,cuyo monto total es de US$1.250 millones para un plazo de 10 aos, del cual el Banco aportar US$1.000 millones y la contrapartida local US$250 millones, financiar parcialmente las necesidades del MTOP en la mejora y expansin de la infraestructura vial; asimismo, apoyar el desarrollo de la capacidad institucional del MTOP lo que permitir administrar eficientemente los recursos, generar una visin sectorial de mediano y largo plazo de las necesidades de la infraestructura vial, y mejorar sustancialmente la gestin de conservacin y mantenimiento en la red vial nacional. El CCLIP tendr las siguientes lneas estratgicas: (i) ampliacin de la capacidad vial; (ii) conservacin del patrimonio vial; (iii) mejora de la gestin vial, particularmente la seguridad vial (sealizacin y puntos crticos) y dar solucin a discontinuidades de la red, y (iv) mejora de la capacidad de planificacin y programacin viales. Se prev que los beneficios resultantes de esta estrategia de actuacin incluyan una mejor integracin fsica de la red vial, mayor accesibilidad y transitabilidad, preservacin del patrimonio vial actual, creciente optimizacin de la gestin de la red vial, y beneficios econmicos de las intervenciones a realizar.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The general objective of the conditional credit line for investment projects (CCLIP) is to help make Ecuadors population more competitive and increase its social and economic integration. The total amount of the CCLIP will be US$1.25 billion for a term of 10 years. Of this amount, the Bank will contribute US$1 billion, and the local counterpart will contribute US$250 million. The CCLIP will partially finance the requirements of the Ministry of Transportation and Public Works (MTOP) to improve and expand the road infrastructure, and will support institutional capacity building for the MTOP to efficiently administer resources, develop a medium- and long-term approach to meeting road infrastructure requirements, and substantially improve management of the preservation and maintenance of the National Road System (NRS). The CCLIP will support the following strategic lines of activity: (i) expansion of road capacity; (ii) preservation of road assets; (iii) better management of the road system, particularly in terms of safety (road signs and critical points) and eliminating discontinuities; and (iv) improved planning and programming capabilities. The expected benefits of the strategy include improved physical integration of the road network, better access and serviceability, preservation of existing road assets, growing optimization of road system management, and the economic benefits from interventions.</narrative>
  </description>
